WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:07.440
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going&nbsp;
to explain an American supernatural drama film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:15.920
called “Nine Days.” Spoilers&nbsp;
ahead! Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:22.400
The movie is set in a dystopian world where&nbsp;
unborn souls are tested for 9 days. If the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:27.760
souls pass the tests, they are given the chance&nbsp;
to live the real world. However, the ones that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:32.640
do not pass the tests, perish forever. The ones&nbsp;
that eventually get to live in the real world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:38.480
have no memory of this interview either.
A man named Will who lives in an isolated house&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:44.400
in the middle of an unknown desert is the arbiter&nbsp;
of souls. Will judges souls and decides which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.840
ones get to inhabit the bodies of living beings.&nbsp;
He interviews souls for a chance to be born in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:55.120
the real world. Not all candidates make the cut&nbsp;
but Will gives them each an experience of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:01.360
choosing before their existence is erased forever.&nbsp;
The only eternal company Will has is a man named&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:07.120
Kyo, a supervisor who makes sure Will selects the&nbsp;
best candidate and assists him with the process.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:12.880
Before becoming an evaluator for unborn souls,&nbsp;
Will previously lived as a normal human, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:18.400
Kyo has never got to live as a living being. 
Will spends most of his time watching and taking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:23.680
notes on a multitude of old fashioned television&nbsp;
screens, each of which displays the life of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:28.480
different individual that Will previously&nbsp;
selected. Among all the souls he has chosen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:34.880
a 28-year old violin prodigy named Amanda is&nbsp;
his favourite. One day, while on her way to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:41.120
concerto, Amanda drives very fast on the highway&nbsp;
and crashes into an overpass, resulting in her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:46.480
death. Will is devastated by her death and&nbsp;
watches old videos of hers for comfort.
&nbsp;

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:50.880
However, Will doesn’t get much time to&nbsp;
mourn Amanda’s death and the following day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.760
new candidates begin arriving to interview&nbsp;
for the vacancy Amanda left behind. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:02.800
candidates include Kane, Anne, Alexander, Mike&nbsp;
and others. The interview lasts for nine days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:06.640
during which Will would test their&nbsp;
personalities and character. He asks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:11.680
the candidates simple questions about life and&nbsp;
has them take notes on what they like or dislike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.880
about the lives of others who were chosen. 
On the first day, Will briefs the candidates about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:22.400
the whole process before starting the interview.&nbsp;
Some candidates are more curious than others. Kane&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:28.080
asks Will the difference between being here and&nbsp;
being alive. When Will reveals that any feeling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:34.080
sensation, emotion is much less intense here than&nbsp;
in real life, Kane asks him how he is sure about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:39.520
that and Will is forced to admit that he has&nbsp;
the experience of living as a person. Curious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:44.800
Kane asks what Will achieved as a living person&nbsp;
but Will shuts him down, saying he can’t divulge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:50.000
any more personal details. Everyone answers the&nbsp;
question in their own way. After finishing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.520
interviews, Will and Kyo get on with their daily&nbsp;
tasks. Later that evening, the last candidate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.520 --> 00:03:01.120
Emma shows up late for the interview. Will is&nbsp;
annoyed by Emma’s tardiness but Kyo convinces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:06.400
him to let her give the interview. Emma is just&nbsp;
as inquisitive as Kane and she asks if Kyo is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:12.960
Will’s boss but Kyo quickly corrects her and jokes&nbsp;
that if he was he would never hire Will. Emma also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:17.440
learns that Kyo has never been alive. 
Will then asks her the same moral dilemma&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:23.200
question but Emma refuses to answer because in&nbsp;
both instances her son dies. Will tells her that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:27.840
she must answer the question because that’s how&nbsp;
the question is supposed to be. Emma puts forth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:33.360
her own question and asks if that’s how the&nbsp;
question is or that’s how cruel the world is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:38.640
Emma and Will both refuse to answer each other's&nbsp;
question and the interview comes to an end. 
&nbsp;

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.480
The next day, Will gives the selected&nbsp;
candidates a tour of the house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:47.840
including the control room from where Will and Kyo&nbsp;
keep an eye of the previously selected candidates.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:52.880
He gives the candidate a task to observe people&nbsp;
on the TV and make notes on a living being of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:58.640
their choice. While observing a living being, Will&nbsp;
notices Mike drawing on his notebook. When Will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:03.440
asks to see it, Mike is initially hesitant&nbsp;
but eventually allows Will to see his art.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:07.840
It is a beautiful sketch of a beach. 
Later, Will goes through each of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:12.960
notebooks and assesses them. All of them have&nbsp;
written about one specific moment of their choice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:17.840
except Emma, who has written about a little bit&nbsp;
of everything. He then individually returns their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:23.120
notebook back in person. Will advises Emma&nbsp;
that she could be more selective. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:28.720
Emma can never be bound by anyone. She asks him&nbsp;
if the candidates he selected remember him. Will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:34.720
answers in a negative but he also mentions Amanda&nbsp;
momentarily remembering him in her childhood. 
&nbsp;

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:39.600
Meanwhile, Kane asks Will if there’s any&nbsp;
area in which he should work on. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:44.480
Will tells him not to think that way. Will says he&nbsp;
doesn’t want Kane to do what Will thinks is right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:49.760
he wants Kane to do what he deep down feels&nbsp;
is right. Not satisfied by his response,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:54.400
Kane points out how Will is going to judge him&nbsp;
in the end anyway and asks Will to tell him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:59.440
the rules so he could play the game better. 
As expected, Will doesn’t reveal the rules and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:04.480
he gives the candidates new assignments. He asks&nbsp;
the candidates to pick a moment they didn’t like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:08.000
from what they saw on the screen.
After examining their answers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:13.360
Will decides to eliminate Mike. A tearful Mike&nbsp;
asks what he did wrong but Will gives him his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:18.400
same standard answer. Will tries to comfort him&nbsp;
and commends him for living every second there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:22.640
with intensity and honesty before asking&nbsp;
him to choose a moment that he wants to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:28.160
experience from what he saw on the TV. 
Later that night, Emma overhears Will and Kyu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:32.480
working in the middle of the night. After learning&nbsp;
that they are working to give Mike a special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:38.320
farewell, Emma offers to help. While working, Kyu&nbsp;
shares that if given a chance, he would love to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:44.320
yell like Tarzan from the top of a mountain. Emma&nbsp;
then asks Will which moment he would choose but an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:49.280
irritated Will doesn’t have time for her questions&nbsp;
and tells her to just focus on the work.
&nbsp;

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:54.480
After finishing the work, Kyu tells Emma that Will&nbsp;
is the only interviewer who gives his candidates a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.480 --> 00:06:00.400
chance to experience a real world moment. He also&nbsp;
reveals that when Will was alive, he was too good,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:05.040
kind and sensitive. Will was talented&nbsp;
but struggled to fit into a world that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:09.120
was different from him. He had so much&nbsp;
love in him but no one to give it to. 
&nbsp;

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:16.240
The next day, Will checks the assignment of the&nbsp;
remaining candidates. Kane tells him about the kid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:21.440
named Rick who is a frequent target of bullies. He&nbsp;
continues that he doesn’t like the fact that Rick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:26.240
doesn’t fight back more than the fact that other&nbsp;
children bully Rick. Kane says that if he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:31.360
in Rick’s place, he would hit the bullies back.&nbsp;
When Will questions him if he justifies violence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:36.880
Kane replies that self defense is justice. 
When it is Emma’s turn, she describes a guy that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:42.000
hates himself. She says that the guy thinks he&nbsp;
is a failure and everything he does is worthless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:46.960
and shameful. Emma says she emphasizes with the&nbsp;
guy for having gone through so much to the point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:51.520
that he just wants to feel nothing anymore.&nbsp;
She further adds that the numbness may make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:57.120
him feel safe but it is also poisoning what’s left&nbsp;
of him. She says that deep inside the man knows it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:02.000
too. Will realises that Emma is describing&nbsp;
him but stops short of acknowledging it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:06.880
He says that the man she is describing sounds&nbsp;
irreparable. Emma quickly responds that the man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:11.680
thinks he is irreparable but she believes that&nbsp;
there’s still something left inside him. 
&nbsp;

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:16.800
Will then excuses himself to bid Mike goodbye.&nbsp;
With the help of Kyu, Emma follows him to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:22.000
secret room where Will gives his candidates their&nbsp;
final experience before they disappear forever.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:27.920
Emma watches in astonishment as Mike experiences&nbsp;
the beach Will created for him. Will then sits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:33.600
with a tearful Mike as he gets lost forever. 
Afterwards, an emotional Will returns to the TV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:38.560
room and sits with Emma. He tells her that when he&nbsp;
was alive he used to be a part of a theatre group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:42.560
in highschool. He reveals he didn’t have&nbsp;
any friends and he once gave a theater&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:47.280
performance that made him feel alive, but&nbsp;
he never pursued his passion after that.
&nbsp;

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:52.240
In between taking interviews, Will continues to&nbsp;
watch old videos of Amanda to figure out how she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:57.680
crashed her car. Will eventually discovers that&nbsp;
Amanda deliberately crashed her car and committed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:02.800
suicide. Will is shocked by the revelation&nbsp;
and blames himself for sending Amanda into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:09.280
cruel world unprepared. As a result, Will starts&nbsp;
fearing a similar fate for a kind hearted Emma.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:13.440
He gives her tough scenarios but she&nbsp;
always chooses kindness and love. 
&nbsp;

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:18.480
During the course of the interview, Maria falls&nbsp;
in love with Will. She writes him a letter and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:23.840
expresses her love. However, Will turns her&nbsp;
down and eliminates her. After experiencing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:28.960
her final moment, Maria breaks into tears and&nbsp;
pleads with Will to give their love a chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:34.480
but Will heartlessly watches her disappear into&nbsp;
the air. All of this leads to Will and Kyu getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:39.840
into an argument. Kyu accuses Will of shutting&nbsp;
himself off and confronts him about his intentions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:44.880
to eliminate a good candidate like Emma. Will&nbsp;
argues that he can’t keep sending flowers to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:50.560
the real world while other interviewers send pigs&nbsp;
that eat them. They eventually cool down and again&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:56.080
start discussing Amanda. Will admits that just&nbsp;
like him, Amanda must have felt immense pain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.080 --> 00:09:00.080
that no one could see with their eyes.
Will ultimately decides to burn all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:04.640
Amanda’s tapes and move on. Moreover,&nbsp;
over the course of the next few days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:09.520
most of the candidates are dismissed for various&nbsp;
reasons, such as self-consciousness and lack of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:16.240
respect for suffering. The candidates are narrowed&nbsp;
down to two: Emma and Kane. On the ninth day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:21.440
Emma finally meets Kane. They both are&nbsp;
contrasting in character. Emma is carefree,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:26.800
kind, and sees the best in people, Kane is more&nbsp;
pessimistic, recognizing the evil in the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:31.920
and showing resolve to fight back against it.&nbsp;
Over dinner, the two get to know each other. 
&nbsp;

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:35.760
Will makes the two sit in a room together&nbsp;
and asks them to tell each other why they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:40.640
shouldn’t be alive. This naturally makes&nbsp;
Emma uncomfortable and she walks out. 
&nbsp;

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:45.920
Later, despite Kyo recommending that Will&nbsp;
pick Emma, Will chooses Kane to be born.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:50.880
Will offers Emma a last experience and she&nbsp;
writes something down on a paper. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:55.760
Emma writes something which Will can’t seem to&nbsp;
do. Will asks her to choose something else but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.760 --> 00:10:01.840
she declines a last experience. As Emma prepares&nbsp;
to leave, Will sees Kane off to the real world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:07.840
Emma asks to see Will one last time but he decides&nbsp;
not to see her off. Kyo offers to be with her in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:13.120
her last moments but she declines and opts to&nbsp;
walk across the desert until she disappears. 
&nbsp;

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:18.720
After Emma leaves Will finds a note from Emma&nbsp;
where she thanks him for everything. She expresses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:23.840
regret for all the things he went through because&nbsp;
of which he doesn’t allow himself to feel alive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:28.800
She tells him that she has written all the&nbsp;
beautiful memories she made in the last 9 days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:34.400
all over the house. She asks him to not take&nbsp;
those moments for granted before signing off.
&nbsp;

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:39.360
Puzzled, Will looks around and finds them written&nbsp;
all over the house. Those moments are a day at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:45.360
the beach, Kyo yelling off a cliff, Laughing&nbsp;
with Kane, a bicycle ride, and many others.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:49.680
Will suddenly realizes that those were&nbsp;
indeed happy moments. Feeling regret,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:55.360
he runs out after Emma. He eventually catches&nbsp;
up to her and passionately recites selections&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.360 --> 00:11:01.200
from Walt Whitman’s Song of Myself, thanking her&nbsp;
for daring him to allow himself to breathe.
&nbsp;

